# 詞: 睇怕

1. 睇怕佢今日又會遲到啦，朝早鬧鐘都響咗好幾次都未起身。 (I'm afraid he'll be late again today; his alarm has gone off several times this morning and he still hasn't gotten up.)
2. 個天黑到咁，睇怕一陣間會落大雨，帶定把遮穩陣啲。 (The sky is so dark, it looks like it's going to rain heavily soon; better bring an umbrella to be safe.)
3. 佢份人咁硬頸，睇怕都唔會聽你嘅勸告。 (He is so stubborn; I'm afraid he won't listen to your advice.)
4. 呢個工程咁大，睇怕要幾個月先至搞得掂。 (This project is so massive; it looks like it will take a few months to get it done.)
5. 睇怕佢已經忘記咗我哋嘅約會，打個電話畀佢提醒下啦。 (I'm afraid he has already forgotten our appointment; let's give him a call to remind him.)
6. 佢最近成日掛住打機唔溫書，睇怕今次考試成績好極有個譜。 (He has been obsessed with gaming and hasn't studied lately; I'm afraid his exam results this time won't be very good.)
7. 呢度塞車塞到咁勁，睇怕我哋趕唔切喺七點前到達會場。 (The traffic jam here is so severe; it looks like we won't make it to the venue before 7 o'clock.)
8. 睇怕呢間餐廳今日已經滿座喇，我哋去隔籬嗰間食啦。 (It looks like this restaurant is fully booked today; let's go eat at the one next door.)
9. 佢尋日發燒發到咁高，睇怕今日都要請假喺屋企休息。 (He had such a high fever yesterday; I'm afraid he'll have to take a day off to rest at home today.)
10. 睇怕你唔肯講出真相，我都係自己查清楚好過。 (I'm afraid you're not willing to tell the truth; I'd better investigate it myself.) [end of text]


